## What I added

The `.srt` file remains the canonical transcript artifact (translations get spliced into it live), so VTT is generated on demand from it — this works retroactively for every existing session and can never go stale waiting for a late translation.

- `server/session/vtt.ts` — `srtToVtt()`: prepends the `WEBVTT` header, converts `HH:MM:SS,mmm` to `HH:MM:SS.mmm` on timestamp lines, and keeps cue numbers as VTT cue identifiers, speaker prefixes, and translation lines intact.
- `GET /api/sessions/:id/vtt` in `server/session/routes.ts` — serves `text/vtt` with `Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="<id>.vtt"`, 404 for unknown sessions.
- `.vtt` download button on the Review page header row (visible when the session has cues), via `sessionsApi.vttUrl()`.
- Tests: `server/session/vtt.test.ts` for the converter (timestamps, translation lines, commas in text, empty transcript) and a route test in `server/app.test.ts` covering headers, body, and the 404.
- README bullet documenting the export.
